// BT-3935: `self do: [...]` in a class method, where the class defines `do:`
// class-side, re-enters the class's own process. It must raise a structured
// `dispatch_error`, not a raw `calling_self` exit. (A block that assigns a
// captured local there is a compile-time escaping-block error.)

TestCase subclass: ClassSideSelfCollectionSendTest

  testSelfDoInClassMethodRaisesStructuredError =>
    self should: [
      ClassSideSelfCollectionProbe countViaSelfDo
    ] raise: #dispatch_error
